# Everything the tools produce: frames saved with `s`, the plots and the CSV
# from probe, the printable tag sheet. Regenerated on demand, tens of
# megabytes within a few sessions, and only ever interesting for the few
# minutes you are looking at one. All of it lands in captures/ so the repo
# root stays readable; the patterns stay too, for anything written by hand.
captures/
*.png
*.csv
*.pdf

# Calibration and learning. All of it describes this rig at this moment
# rather than the project, all of it is rewritten as the tools run, and
# tag_reference.json changes on literally every frame. Deliberately not
# tracked: a repo that is dirty after every run is a repo nobody commits to.
#
# Losing them costs one --reclick, one --dial-exposure and one --teach.
corners.json
warp.json
camera.json
exposure.json
tag_reference.json
prototypes.json

# Built from github.com/jtfrey/uvc-util, which is not ours to vendor, and a
# Mac-only binary besides. setup.py --tools builds it.
uvc-util

# Working notes, kept on disk and out of a public repo. HANDOVER.md is the
# original brief, PLAN.md the state, LOG.md the reasoning and measurements
# behind every decision. README.md is the only one meant for other people.
HANDOVER.md
PLAN.md
LOG.md

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.venv/
.gstack/

# Local Netlify folder
.netlify
